{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794746692,"nonce":"QAv9XH/Z39iTt7R0im8SzSuD+gA=","title":"Libraries on different hxn versions resolve one hxn haxelib by -lib order, silently","message":"A program using two hx-n libraries whose haxelib.json depend on different hxn versions gets the hxn haxelib of whichever `-lib` comes first, with no warning. Reproducer, with hxn-window 0.1.1 (hxn 0.3.1) and hxn-gpu-vulkan 0.1.0 (hxn 0.3.2) installed:\n\n    haxe -lib hxn-window -lib hxn-gpu-vulkan -main Main -hl m.hl\n    (unknown) : Type not found : gpu.vulkan.Shaders\n\n`haxelib path` resolves hxn to 0.3.1, whose `hxn.Bind.lib` does not add a package's `sources/` to the class path, so the driver's `init` macro cannot find its class. With the `-lib` order swapped it compiles, on 0.3.2. hxn-window and hxn-av 0.1.2 move to hxn 0.3.2, which removes this case, but the next hxn release reopens it for any library not yet rebuilt.\n\n`hxn.Bind.lib` knows which hxn the package was generated for (its haxelib.json dependency). It could fail the build, naming both versions and the libraries, when the hxn haxelib in use is a different version, or accept any 0.3.x where the generated code is compatible.","files":null}]}